Problem Reduction to Max Flow Complexity Bipartite Matching Construct a flow network with source connected to left partition and sink connected to right partition, edges represent possible matches. O(E√V) Edge Disjoint Paths Construct a flow network where each edge has capacity 1, find max flow from source to sink. O(E√V) Vertex Disjoint Paths Split each vertex into two vertices connected by an edge of capacity 1, find max flow. O(E√V) Circulation with Demands Transform the problem into a flow network with lower and upper bounds on edges, check if max flow equals total demand. O(E√V) Project Selection Construct a flow network where projects are nodes, edges represent dependencies, and capacities represent profits or costs. O(E√V) Baseball Elimination Construct a flow network where teams are nodes, edges represent games left to play, and capacities represent possible wins. O(E√V) <p>Bipartite Matching via Flow:</p> <pre><code>int bipartiteViaFlow(int leftN, int rightN, vector&lt;pair&lt;int,int&gt;&gt;&amp; edges){
    int totalN = leftN + rightN + 2;
    int S = totalN - 2; 
    int T = totalN - 1;
    Dinic d(totalN);
    for(int i = 0; i &lt; leftN; i++){
        d.add_edge(S, i, 1);
    }
    for(int i = 0; i &lt; rightN; i++){
        d.add_edge(leftN + i, T, 1);
    }
    for(auto &amp;edge : edges){
        int u = edge.first;
        int v = edge.second;
        d.add_edge(u, leftN + v, 1);
    }
    return d.max_flow(S, T);
}
</code></pre>

Objective Relaxation Heap Min-sum <code>dist[v] = min(dist[v], dist[u] + w)</code> Min-heap Max-min <code>dist[v] = max(dist[v], min(dist[u], w))</code> Max-heap Min-max <code>dist[v] = min(dist[v], max(dist[u], w))</code> Min-heap Max-product <code>dist[v] = max(dist[v], dist[u] * w)</code> Max-heap <p>Template (Max-Min Dijkstra e.g., LC 2812):</p> <pre><code>int maxMinDijkstra(vector&lt;vector&lt;int&gt;&gt;&amp; safety, int n) {
    vector&lt;vector&lt;int&gt;&gt; dist(n, vector&lt;int&gt;(n, 0));
    dist[0][0] = safety[0][0];
    priority_queue&lt;tuple&lt;int,int,int&gt;&gt; pq;
    pq.push({safety[0][0], 0, 0});
    int dirs[4][2] = {{0,1},{0,-1},{1,0},{-1,0}};
    while (!pq.empty()) {
        auto [d, r, c] = pq.top(); pq.pop();
        if (r == n-1 &amp;&amp; c == n-1) return d;
        if (d &lt; dist[r][c]) continue;
        for (auto&amp; dir : dirs) {
            int nr = r+dir[0], nc = c+dir[1];
            if (nr&gt;=0 &amp;&amp; nr&lt;n &amp;&amp; nc&gt;=0 &amp;&amp; nc&lt;n) {
                int newDist = min(d, safety[nr][nc]);
                if (newDist &gt; dist[nr][nc]) {
                    dist[nr][nc] = newDist;
                    pq.push({newDist, nr, nc});
                }
            }
        }
    }
    return 0;
}

</code></pre>
